1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:05,040
After heavy rain, a cocoa grower has about thirty minutes to scout.

2
00:00:05,090 --> 00:00:07,000
Which blocks should they check first?

3
00:00:07,050 --> 00:00:11,080
Guess wrong, and black pod spreads to healthy pods.

4
00:00:12,300 --> 00:00:18,550
Black pod spreads by rain splash and costs an estimated twenty to thirty percent of global cocoa production.

5
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:23,210
Heavy rain is already linked to lower yields in Ghana, Ecuador and Indonesia.

6
00:00:23,260 --> 00:00:31,210
In Malaysia, eighty-six percent of cocoa land is smallholdings, and advisers can't visit every farm after every storm.

7
00:00:32,020 --> 00:00:36,050
Growers already have photo apps, forecasts and paper logs.

8
00:00:36,100 --> 00:00:41,220
But none of them turns "it rained heavily" into "walk these blocks first, in the time you have".

9
00:00:41,270 --> 00:00:45,000
That empty corner is where KokoShield sits.

10
00:00:45,680 --> 00:00:53,680
KokoShield Field Desk combines the rain reading, the block map and past cases into a ranked route that fits thirty minutes.

11
00:00:53,730 --> 00:00:58,310
Every stop shows why it's there, on a phone or a printed checklist.

12
00:01:00,020 --> 00:01:03,720
Scouts log each suspected pod with a note and a photo.

13
00:01:03,770 --> 00:01:09,820
An adviser then confirms or rules out every case, so only verified disease counts.

14
00:01:10,600 --> 00:01:13,860
Our pilot runs on one cocoa farm in Tanjung Sepat.

15
00:01:13,910 --> 00:01:19,150
Two scouts walk the same thirty minutes: one on the ranked route, one on the usual round.

16
00:01:19,200 --> 00:01:21,680
A follow-up check counts what each missed.

17
00:01:21,730 --> 00:01:26,810
We go ahead only if the ranked route finds more confirmed pods per hour in three of four rounds.

18
00:01:26,860 --> 00:01:29,970
The pilot budget is twelve hundred ringgit.

19
00:01:30,860 --> 00:01:35,600
Finding disease sooner means fewer pods lost, and treatment only where it's needed.

20
00:01:35,650 --> 00:01:37,830
Growers use KokoShield for free.

21
00:01:37,880 --> 00:01:46,600
A cooperative or buyer pays seventy-five ringgit per farm per season, starting with a twenty-farm cluster in Sabah or Sarawak in 2027.

22
00:01:47,370 --> 00:01:49,910
We're a team of five from Universiti Malaya.

23
00:01:49,960 --> 00:01:58,410
KokoShield helps cocoa growers find disease sooner after the rain: one farm first, then every cocoa region facing wetter seasons.
